# The working directories a run leaves beside the checkout, at the ROOT and only
# there. Anchored with a leading slash, because a bare "data/" matches a
# directory of that name at every depth: it swallowed tests/data - the 180
# recorded CLI pages and every other fixture the suite READS - so a fresh clone
# collected the suite and failed it, while the machine that wrote the fixtures
# stayed green.
/legacy/
/data/
/temp/
/logs/
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/

# setuptools' staging tree and its metadata: a second copy of every module in
# the package, regenerated by every build.
build/
*.egg-info/

# Editor and OS droppings. None of them belong to the project, and the two
# machines this is edited on leave different ones.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The Windows yt-dlp: the ytdlp command picks a yt-dlp.exe up from the checkout
# root, and it is a 17 MB binary each machine downloads for itself.
yt-dlp.exe
